module gunbc.rung_drop_amendment.regen_determinism_waived_by_operator_ruling

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop_amendment { RungDropAmendment }

data regen_determinism_waived_by_operator_ruling: RungDropAmendment = RungDropAmendment {
  drop_identity: "floor_cut_regen_second_generation_agreement" as NonEmptyStr,

  amended: "2026-10-04",

  later_event: "operator ruling (paraphrased: the regen need not run multiple times, and v1 determinism is no longer a concern). Between 2026-09-23 and 2026-10-04 the stage0 mirror half of this capability WAS enrolled, as the `regen-fixed-point` phase of the build lane (a same-binary second emit compared against the first generation's receipt); the registry-projection half never was, so this row stood throughout. The ruling deletes that phase AND the `--required-regen-fixed-point` mode behind it, so nothing now detects a nondeterministic v1 emitter on any path. That is not a lower rung -- the ladder has none below mitigatable -- it is a scope decision: BY OPERATOR RULING 2026-10-04, v1 SEED-EMIT NONDETERMINISM IS OUTSIDE THE MODELED GUARANTEE. REASON: the second generation cost a whole-closure emit on every required run and on every author regen while v1 is frozen-semantics seed maintenance, and the operator judged determinism of that seed not worth the price.",

  bearing: "A waiver of DETERMINISM only: CONVERGENCE (the committed mirrors equal one emission by the seed built from them) stays enforced by the generated-artifact phase. The row is NOT retired -- its trigger has not fired, and a ruling that the capability is not owed is not that trigger."
}
